\subsection{Evaluation}

The dataset is evaluated using the BLEU score \cite{papineni2002bleu}.

\subsection{Baseline}

The baseline is a simple LSTM model with a single layer of 256 units.

\subsection{Results}

\end{itemize}

\subsection{Dataset}

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Dataset:} We use the CNN/Daily Mail dataset \cite{hermann2015teaching} for our experiments. The dataset consists of news articles and their corresponding summaries. The dataset is split into three parts: training, validation and test. The training set contains 287,226 samples, the validation set contains 13,368 samples and the test set contains 11,490 samples.

\end{itemize}

\subsection{Evaluation}

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Human Evaluation}

    We conducted human evaluation on the generated summaries. We randomly sampled 100 examples from the test set and asked three annotators to evaluate the summaries. The annotators were asked to rate the summaries on a scale of 1 to 5, where 1 means the summary is completely irrelevant to the source text and 5 means the summary is completely relevant to the source text.

\end{itemize}

\subsection{Dataset}

We use the same dataset as \citet{zhang-etal-2019-pegasus} for the summarization task. The dataset contains 1,000 news articles from CNN and Daily Mail, and the corresponding summaries. We use the same preprocessing steps as \citet{zhang-etal-2019-pegasus} to obtain the dataset.

\subsection{Implementation Details}

\subsection{Dataset}

We use the CNN/Daily Mail dataset \cite{hermann2015teaching} for our experiments. The dataset consists of news articles and their corresponding summaries. The dataset is split into three parts: training, validation, and test. The training set contains 287,226 pairs of articles and summaries, the validation set contains 13,368 pairs, and the test set contains 11,490 pairs. The average length of the articles is 788 words, and the average length of the summaries is 58 words.

